.TH MODBUS-SCRAPER-CLI 1 "2026-11-05" "pv-suite 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
modbus-scraper-cli \- console-style session on the modbus-scraper
control server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modbus-scraper-cli
.RI [ options ]
.IB command " [args ...]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
One client, three modes by the invocation shape: command words one-shot
(\fBmodbus-scraper-cli\fR show config\fR \(em the raw verdict head prints,
exit 0 ok, 1 connection error, 2 misuse), piped stdin batch (the script lines
run in order, the same raw faces), a bare terminal the interactive console.
.PP
A session front-end on top of modbus-scraper's JSON-lines control socket:
prompt with the connected port, TAB completion and \fB?\fR in every
position (with the short descriptions from the shared command registry),
\fBset\fR commands print only the confirmation, \fBshow <setting>\fR
prints the bare value, \fBinspect\fR dumps the state, and
\fBshutdown\fR asks before it stops the scraper. When the connection dies
mid-session the console
retries (\fB--reconnect\fR attempts, \fB--reconnect-wait\fR seconds
apart). With a control token configured the wire is HMAC-signed: the
console signs every command and verifies every reply.
.PP
Every reply prints through the console's pager: a text taller than the
screen pauses at a page \(em space prints the next page, return one more
line, \fBq\fR stops the rest (the command already ran; only the
rendering stops). \fB--page-size\fR/\fBCLI_PAGE_SIZE\fR set the page
size (\fB0\fR = off, empty = the terminal height); a session-local
\fBpage\fR command retunes it live (never sent to the daemon); a
terminal smaller than 20 rows or 64 columns refuses to start.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-control\-port
control server target: unix socket path or TCP port on 127.0.0.1,
auto\-detected (env CTL when unset) — same flag as the scraper itself
.TP
.B command
one\-shot control command, e.g. inspect, show config, set interval 5,
request poll now, request reload, request restart, shutdown (bare: piped
stdin batch\-runs a script, a terminal opens the console)
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
socket timeout in seconds
.TP
.BI \-\-reconnect " N"
console only: when the connection dies (an unanswered ping, a reset, a
timeout), retry this many times before giving up; 0 = off
.TP
.BI \-\-reconnect\-wait " N"
console only: seconds between the reconnect attempts
.TP
.B \-\-control\-token
control auth token for TCP (env CONTROL_TOKEN); a file:<path> value
reads the first line of an owner\-only 0600 file
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-log
audit trail: a file path, \- for stdout, or none for no local file (the
forward carries the trail); the XDG state home when unset
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-forward
also forward every audit line: none, syslog, syslog:/path,
udp://host[:port] or tcp://host[:port] (the off\-box copy,
docs/SECURITY.md)
.TP
.B \-\-audit\-forward\-format
the remote forward's envelope: rfc5424 (the default) or cef — the local
syslog forms keep the verbatim send
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-max\-mb " N"
rotate the audit log at this size, 0 = off
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-files " N"
rotated audit backups to keep
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audit\-log
disable the audit trail
.TP
.BI \-\-page\-size " N"
console pager: N lines per page (0 = off, empty = the terminal height;
env CLI_PAGE_SIZE)


.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTL
the control target when \fB--control-port\fR is unset.
.TP
.B CONTROL_TOKEN ", " CLI_KEEPALIVE
the TCP token and the idle-ping interval in seconds (0 = off).
.TP
.B CLI_PAGE_SIZE
the console pager's page size, lines; \fB0\fR = off, empty = the
terminal height.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the session ended cleanly.
.TP
.B 1
connection or control error.
.TP
.B 2
command-line misuse.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR modbus-scraper (1)
